        <div id="taste" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            8. What Do Buyers Say About Rule 1 Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Taste is the part of Rule 1 the brand leans on hardest, and it is the part we cannot judge for you, because we did not taste these powders. What we can say is what the formula predicts and what the brand and its listings show. R1 Protein is an isolate with lecithin and no gums, which in general means a thinner shake that dissolves quickly in water; the Whey Protein blend adds concentrate, cellulose gum and xanthan gum, which usually means a thicker, creamier drink.
          </p>

          <p>
            The customer quotes Rule 1 chooses to feature lean on flavor. One on the Whey Protein page reads, "I always come back to Rule 1 for the best flavor out there," and the R1 Protein page quotes a buyer calling it "top of the line." Those are hand-picked testimonials, so read them as marketing, not as a survey. Before buying a full 5 lb tub in a new flavor, read the most recent reviews on the specific Amazon listing for that flavor, because flavor feedback varies far more than the label does.
          </p>

          <p>
            The flavor range is wide enough that most people will find something. R1 Protein lists 19 flavors on the brand site: Chocolate Fudge, Milk Chocolate, Dark Chocolate, Cafe Mocha, Chocolate Peanut Butter, Mint Chocolate Chip, Cookies and Creme, Salted Caramel, Birthday Cake, Fruity Cereal, Banana Creme, Strawberries and Creme, Strawberry Banana, Orange Dreamsicle, Pistachio Ice Cream, Vanilla Creme, Vanilla Butter Cake, Pure Vanilla and Unflavored. The blend adds Vanilla Ice Cream, Campfire Smores and Toasted Cinnamon Cereal.
          </p>

          <p>
            For mixing, Rule 1's directions say about one scoop with 6 to 8 oz of cold water, milk or another drink, in a shaker cup or a glass with a spoon. Isolates generally mix well with a spoon; the blend and the casein, with their gums, do better in a shaker. If sweetness is your complaint with any protein, try more liquid first, or mix a scoop of Unflavored into a flavored scoop to cut the sucralose. Our <a href="/best-tasting-protein-powder/">best tasting protein powder</a> guide covers flavors buyers rate highly across brands.
          </p>
